module test.claim.scm_commit_closure_json_v2_witness

// The durable repository image, executed. The claim under test is that a store survives the round
// trip to text and back AS THE SAME PROGRAM, and that every way the text can lie REFUSES rather than
// producing a plausible store.
//
// The identity claims here are the load-bearing ones. The image carries NO object identities -- see
// gunbc.scm.commit_closure_json_v2's header for why -- so what these witnesses establish is that identity survives
// anyway, because it is re-derived from structure on load. A round trip that merely produced "some
// store" would satisfy a weaker test; comparing the reconstructed PROGRAM through checkout is what
// makes it a claim about meaning rather than about bytes.
//
// Every claim is paired with a discriminating control, and the controls are the point: a decoder
// that refused unconditionally would pass all seven refusal claims, and a comparison that could not
// say no would pass the round trip.

